# Build context for the Dockerfile in this directory.
#
# The Dockerfile finishes with `COPY . .`, so every file left in the context is
# uploaded to the daemon before the first `RUN` and re-sent on every rebuild.
# Everything below is either reinstalled by `npm ci`, regenerated by
# `npm run build`, or irrelevant to a production image.
#
# Patterns are given both bare and as `**/name` on purpose: the bare form covers
# the repo root, the glob covers per-workspace copies (apps/web/node_modules,
# apps/web/.next, apps/web/coverage, ...).

# --- Dependencies: the image runs `npm ci` itself ------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Build output: regenerated by `npm run build` ------------------------
# The workspace packages in packages/* point `main` at `src/index.ts` and have
# no build step, so there is no committed dist/ and nothing to lose here.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
out
**/out
**/.turbo
.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
**/next-env.d.ts

# --- Test, coverage and browser-run artifacts ----------------------------
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
.playwright
**/.playwright
.playwright-cli
**/.playwright-cli

# --- Version control, editor and agent tooling ---------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.agents
.freebuff
.cloud-attachments
.impeccable
.serena
.postman
.shots
.scratch
.vercel

# --- Local secrets and certificates: never into an image layer -----------
# Note: there is no `!.env.example` exception. The template holds placeholders
# only, and nothing in the build reads it.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key

# --- OS noise, logs and editor backups -----------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
**/*.log
*.bak
**/*.bak
*.orig
**/*.orig
*.rej
**/*.rej
